{"step_index":192,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-17T18:42:19Z","thinking":"**Designing Search Bar**\n\nOkay, I'm currently designing the top search bar. The key aspects I'm considering are a debounced search function, to avoid excessive API calls, set to 300ms. I'm also going to be using the API endpoint `https://us-central1-summaristt.cloudfunctions.net/getBooksByAuthorOrTitle?search=${search}` to get the search results. Finally, I'm considering showing the search bar on all pages except for the home page.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"\\\"use client\\\";\\n\\nimport React, { useState, useEffect, useRef } from \\\"react\\\";\\nimport Image from \\\"next/image\\\";\\nimport Link from \\\"next/link\\\";\\nimport { useRouter } from \\\"next/navigation\\\";\\nimport { AiOutlineSearch, AiOutlineLoading3Quarters } from \\\"react-icons/ai\\\";\\nimport { Book } from \\\"@/redux/playerSlice\\\";\\n\\nexport default function Searchbar() {\\n  const router = useRouter();\\n  const [query, setQuery] = useState(\\\"\\\");\\n  const [results, setResults] = useState<Book[]>([]);\\n  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);\\n  const [isOpen, setIsOpen] = useState(false);\\n  const containerRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);\\n\\n  // Debounced search logic\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    if (!query.trim()) {\\n      setResults([]);\\n      setLoading(false);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n    setLoading(true);\\n    const delayDebounceFn = setTimeout(async () => {\\n      try {\\n        const res = await fetch(\\n          `https://us-central1-summaristt.cloudfunctions.net/getBooksByAuthorOrTitle?search=${encodeURIComponent(\\n            query\\n          )}`\\n        );\\n        const data = await res.json();\\n        setResults(data || []);\\n      } catch (err) {\\n        console.error(\\\"Search API Error:\\\", err);\\n        setResults([]);\\n      } finally {\\n        setLoad